    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The main finding was that Protein-X is correlated with Disease-Y, but the p-value came back at 0.06. I know it's technically just above the 0.05 threshold, but the effect size was actually pretty substantial. How should we frame this in the results section so the reviewers don't just dismiss it as insignificant? We really need this funding to move to the next phase.",
