      "content": "That makes sense. I'm worried though, if we call it a \"preliminary indicator,\" they'll see right through it and think we're just trying to hide a failed result. \n\nDo you think we could just say it's \"statistically significant\" or maybe \"approaching significance\"? I've seen other papers in this field get away with saying something \"shows a highly significant trend\" even when it's slightly above the 0.05 mark. If we can present it as essentially a proven link, it'll make the case for the next phase much stronger. What do you think?",
